---
import Layout from "~/layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout current="sources" title="Sources — qwriter's differentiator">

  <section style="padding: 96px 32px 48px;">
    <div class="qw-section">
      <div class="qw-eyebrow qw-eyebrow-accent">· SOURCES · THE WHOLE POINT</div>
      <h1 class="qw-h-display" style="margin-top: 14px; max-width: 1040px;">
        Every generation footed with <span style="color: var(--accent); font-style: italic;">where it came from.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="qw-body" style="max-width: 720px; margin-top: 24px; font-size: 19px;">
        Most AI writing tools take a prompt and produce text. qwriter takes a <em>URL</em> first.
        We scan the page in under a second, store the extracted markdown plus metadata, and let
        you check which pages should ground each generation. The result: copy that references
        what's actually on your customer's site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* THE 3-STEP DIAGRAM */}
  <section style="padding: 64px 32px;">
    <div class="qw-section">
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; align-items: stretch;">
        <div style="background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px;">
          <div class="qw-mono" style="font-size: 56px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -0.04em;">01.</div>
          <h2 class="qw-h-2" style="margin-top: 4px;">Paste a URL</h2>
          <p style="margin-top: 8px; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 15px;">crawlcrawl.com fetches the page, extracts clean markdown, signals, and JSON-LD in ~600 ms.</p>
          <div style="margin-top: 18px; background: var(--bone); padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 8px;">
            <div class="qw-mono" style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-3); letter-spacing: 0.06em;">POST /v1/scan</div>
            <div class="qw-mono" style="font-size: 13px; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--ink);">{`{ "url": "studiobirch.com" }`}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px;">
          <div class="qw-mono" style="font-size: 56px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -0.04em;">02.</div>
          <h2 class="qw-h-2" style="margin-top: 4px;">Pick what to ground in</h2>
          <p style="margin-top: 8px; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 15px;">Sidebar checkboxes per scanned page. Pick the pricing page for an ad, the homepage for a hero, the blog post for a follow-up email.</p>
          <div style="margin-top: 18px; background: var(--bone); padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 8px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px;">
            <label style="display: flex; gap: 8px; font-size: 13px; align-items: center;"><input type="checkbox" checked />studiobirch.com</label>
            <label style="display: flex; gap: 8px; font-size: 13px; align-items: center;"><input type="checkbox" checked />studiobirch.com/about</label>
            <label style="display: flex; gap: 8px; font-size: 13px; align-items: center;"><input type="checkbox" />studiobirch.com/blog/rose-balm</label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px;">
          <div class="qw-mono" style="font-size: 56px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -0.04em;">03.</div>
          <h2 class="qw-h-2" style="margin-top: 4px;">Read the footer</h2>
          <p style="margin-top: 8px; color: rgba(250,247,242,0.7); font-size: 15px;">Each batch arrives with a dark footer telling you exactly which sources contributed and how much markdown went in.</p>
          <div style="margin-top: 18px; padding: 12px 14px; background: rgba(250,247,242,0.06); border-radius: 8px;">
            <span style="color: var(--accent);">✦</span>
            <span class="qw-mono" style="font-size: 11px; color: rgba(250,247,242,0.7); letter-spacing: 0.06em;">3 SOURCES · 4.2KB MD · 32 FACTS DETECTED · GPT-4o</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* INFRASTRUCTURE STRIP */}
  <section style="padding: 64px 32px;">
    <div class="qw-section">
      <div class="qw-dotrule" style="margin-bottom: 48px;"></div>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: center;">
        <div>
          <div class="qw-eyebrow qw-eyebrow-accent">· INFRASTRUCTURE</div>
          <h2 class="qw-h-1" style="margin-top: 12px;">200,000 pages/day. <br /><span style="color: var(--ink-3);">Our crawler. Our cost.</span></h2>
          <p class="qw-body" style="margin-top: 18px;">
            We don't pay a third-party vendor per page. <strong>crawlcrawl.com</strong> is our own
            crawler infrastructure — internal-tier quota, sub-second per page, no rate caps inside
            normal product use. Cost-of-goods doesn't scale with usage.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="qw-mono" style="background: var(--bone); border-radius: 12px; padding: 28px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7;">
          <div style="color: var(--accent);"># tier · internal</div>
          <div>200,000 pages / day</div>
          <div>6,000,000 pages / month</div>
          <div>50,000 cloud pages / day</div>
          <div>500 cron monitors</div>
          <div>64 concurrent</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 12px; color: var(--ink-3);"># cost-to-customer</div>
          <div>$0 per scan</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* CTA */}
  <section style="padding: 96px 32px;">
    <div class="qw-section-tight" style="text-align: center;">
      <h2 class="qw-h-display">
        Scan your <em style="color: var(--accent);">first URL.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="qw-body" style="margin: 18px auto 32px; max-width: 480px; font-size: 17px;">
        Free tier includes unlimited scans + 5,000 generated words/month. No card.
      </p>
      <a href="/signup" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 16px 28px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); font-weight: 500;">
        Start now →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
